%%{init: {'flowchart': {'curve': 'linear'}}}%%
%% ==================================================
%% Main Header
%% ==================================================
TITLE["TELECOM WORKFLOW<br/>Estimate–Design (Bid Stage)"]
%% ITB & Basis
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> A

A["ITB and Design Basis Review<br/><br/>
1. Telecom design basis and philosophy reviewed<br/>
2. Telecom specifications and block diagrams reviewed<br/>
3. Indoor and outdoor IP ratings confirmed<br/>
4. Hazardous-area and explosion-proof requirements confirmed<br/>
5. Applicable codes standards and local regulations confirmed<br/>
6. Security regulations confirmed for example Saudi HCIS
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Scope & Interfaces
%% ==================================================
A --> B

B["Scope Interfaces and Existing Systems<br/><br/>
1. Supply and work scope boundaries defined<br/>
2. Expansion and modification interfaces identified<br/>
3. Tie-in points and physical connections identified<br/>
4. Intra-system and inter-system interfaces checked<br/>
5. Existing system capacity and IO ports verified<br/>
6. Site survey requirement confirmed
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Redundancy
%% ==================================================
B --> C

C["Redundancy and Reliability Requirements<br/><br/>
1. Hot standby and cold standby requirements verified<br/>
2. Failover load balancing one-plus-one and N-plus-one verified<br/>
3. Cable redundancy and route diversity verified<br/>
4. SIL-level security requirements verified<br/>
5. Single-system design applied where no requirement exists
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Default Standards
%% ==================================================
C --> D

D["Default Subsystem Standards If ITB Is Silent<br/><br/>
1. Telephone standard defined SIP or H.323<br/>
2. CCTV standard defined IP-based H.264 1080p<br/>
3. PAGA standard defined 100V line Class C amplifier<br/>
4. Radio standard defined TETRA Release 2<br/>
5. ACS standard defined ISO IEC 18000-3 13.56 MHz<br/>
6. Firewall standard defined NIST 800-41<br/>
7. IDPS standard defined NIST 800-94
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Telephone System
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> T

T["Telephone System Design Workflow<br/><br/>
1. Analog or VoIP system selected<br/>
2. MDF-IDF hierarchy applied for analog system<br/>
3. MDF-IDF trunk sized with 25 percent spare<br/>
4. VoIP patch panel ports sized with 25 percent spare<br/>
5. Explosion-proof phones applied in hazardous areas<br/>
6. Outdoor phones checked for IP rating or IP65 default
"]

%% ==================================================
%% CCTV System
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> CCTV

CCTV["CCTV System Design Workflow<br/><br/>
1. Resolution IPS traffic and storage defined<br/>
2. Default applied IP-based H.264 1080p if unspecified<br/>
3. Outdoor cameras checked for IP rating or IP65 default<br/>
4. Sunshade applied for high temperature areas<br/>
5. Explosion-proof cameras applied in hazardous areas<br/>
6. Indoor Cat 6 PoE and outdoor fiber plus power applied
"]

%% ==================================================
%% PAGA System
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> P

P["PAGA System Design Workflow<br/><br/>
1. PA coverage requirement reviewed<br/>
2. Full area coverage applied if unspecified<br/>
3. A-B zoning applied where required<br/>
4. Speaker type selected by noise level and area<br/>
5. Monitoring return cabling included<br/>
6. Speaker junction boxes treated as vendor scope
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Radio System
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> R

R["Radio System Design Workflow<br/><br/>
1. Coverage and licensing responsibility confirmed<br/>
2. Antenna height minimum 30 m applied for plant coverage<br/>
3. GMDSS default coverage applied if required<br/>
4. Antenna tower quantity and height reflected in MR<br/>
5. Indoor repeater applied only if signal below minus 70 dBm<br/>
6. Coaxial cable and antenna accessories treated as vendor scope
"]

%% ==================================================
%% ACS System
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> ACS

ACS["Access Control System Workflow<br/><br/>
1. Door types classified main exit-only and general<br/>
2. Readers applied only to main or security doors if unspecified<br/>
3. Controller to reader uses Cat 6 cabling<br/>
4. Lock button and sensor IO uses 0.65 sqmm cable<br/>
5. Vendor scope clearly identified in MR and BOQ
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Data Network & IDS
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> DN

DN["Data Network and IDS Workflow<br/><br/>
1. Dual 1 Gbps redundancy applied if capacity unspecified<br/>
2. Core distribution and access layers defined<br/>
3. External network connections protected by firewall and IDPS<br/>
4. Single-mode fiber backbone per ITU-T G.652 applied<br/>
5. Default 24-core fiber used if unspecified<br/>
6. IDS field devices arranged in ring or sub-rings
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Cable & MTO
%% ==================================================
DN --> F
ACS --> F
R --> F
P --> F
CCTV --> F
T --> F
F["Cable Rules and MTO Development<br/><br/>
1. Cable MTO derived from block diagrams and layouts<br/>
2. Telecom routes separated from electrical and instrument routes<br/>
3. Default cable types applied per system<br/>
4. Redundancy impact on cable quantities checked<br/>
5. Routes grouped by area and nearest equipment room
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Vendor Scope
%% ==================================================
A --> G
DN --> G
ACS --> G
R --> G
P --> G
CCTV --> G
T --> G
G["Vendor Scope and Interfaces<br/><br/>
1. Vendor-supplied cables and accessories identified<br/>
2. Vendor scope included in MR and BOQ<br/>
3. Vendor quantities verified during TBE<br/>
4. Vendor items marked as By Vendor in BOQ
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Interdiscipline
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> H

H["Interdiscipline Engineering Deliverables<br/><br/>
1. Cable tray loading and routing issued to Process and Civil<br/>
2. Trench duct foundation and manhole data issued to Civil<br/>
3. Telecom equipment heat dissipation issued to HVAC<br/>
4. Telecom grounding targets issued to Electrical
"]

%% ==================================================
%% BOQ Validation
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> I

I["Vendor Packages and BOQ Validation<br/><br/>
1. Vendor issue package prepared and issued<br/>
2. Vendor return package received and reviewed<br/>
3. BOQ validated against vendor quantities<br/>
4. Quantities benchmarked against similar past projects<br/>
5. Revamp and tie-in quantities separated<br/>
6. Latest documents confirmed issued to vendors
"]

%% ==================================================
%% Final Review
%% ==================================================
TITLE --> J

J["Final Estimate-Design Review<br/><br/>
1. Aboveground and underground cable routing verified<br/>
2. Cable sizing derating factors confirmed<br/>
3. All ITB addenda confirmed incorporated<br/>
4. Estimate-design frozen for bid submission
"]

